# These upstream emitters surrender allocations to g_signal_emit(), which only borrows
# its arguments. The allocations leak even with zero listeners. Value-copying boxed
# types hide the original pointer, while refcounted containers share it between all
# listeners. Consuming transfer ownership per listener would invalidate later listeners.
# https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gobject-introspection/-/issues/470
# gimarshallingtests.c:10270-10378 and regress.c:3023-3032 (pinned fixture source).
